---
/**
 * KIMI-LOOPS-K3 — triangle-area topic page: short auto demo, then hands-on.
 *
 * The learner drags the triangle's apex along a line parallel to the base;
 * the shape shears but the area readout stays S = a·h/2 = 6·4/2 = 12.
 *
 *   - demo glides the apex once (≤3 s), only when in view, once per session
 *   - drag: Pointer Events with setPointerCapture, touch-action: none
 *   - keyboard/SR: a real <input type="range"> (arrows work natively),
 *     synced with the SVG handle both ways; aria-live announces the area
 *   - prefers-reduced-motion / html.noam-a11y-motion: no auto demo, no
 *     transitions — dragging keeps working
 *
 * Driven by ../lib/triExplorer.ts.
 */
---

<div class="tri-explorer" data-tri-explorer>
  <div class="tri-explorer__card">
    <svg class="tri-explorer__svg" viewBox="0 0 560 330" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
      {/* the parallel line the apex slides on */}
      <line class="te-parallel" x1="60" y1="92" x2="500" y2="92" />

      {/* triangle (fill under the stroke) */}
      <polygon data-el="poly-fill" class="te-fill" points="150,252 390,252 270,92" />
      <polygon data-el="poly" class="te-line" points="150,252 390,252 270,92" />

      {/* height guide + right-angle mark */}
      <line data-el="height" class="te-dash" x1="270" y1="252" x2="270" y2="92" />
      <path data-el="ra" class="te-line-thin" d="M270 240 L282 240 L282 252" />

      {/* base */}
      <line class="te-line" x1="150" y1="252" x2="390" y2="252" />
      <text class="te-t te-num" x="270" y="278" text-anchor="middle">a = 6</text>
      <text data-el="lbl-h" class="te-t te-num" x="290" y="176">h = 4</text>

      {/* draggable apex handle (visual + generous hit area) */}
      <circle data-el="hit" class="te-hit" cx="270" cy="92" r="30" />
      <circle data-el="handle" class="te-handle" cx="270" cy="92" r="11" />
    </svg>

    <p class="tri-explorer__readout" dir="ltr">
      S = a·h/2 = 6·4/2 = <b class="te-ok">12</b>
    </p>
    <p class="tri-explorer__hint" data-el="hint">
      גררו את הקודקוד ימינה ושמאלה — הבסיס והגובה לא משתנים, וגם השטח נשאר <bdi>12</bdi>
    </p>

    <label class="te-slider">
      <span class="sr-only">מיקום קודקוד המשולש לאורך הקו המקביל לבסיס</span>
      <input
        type="range"
        data-el="range"
        min="-1.5"
        max="8"
        step="0.1"
        value="3"
        aria-describedby="te-readout-note"
      />
    </label>
    <p class="sr-only" id="te-readout-note">שטח המשולש הוא 12 בכל מיקום של הקודקוד</p>
    <p class="sr-only" aria-live="polite" data-el="live"></p>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
  import { initTriExplorers } from '../lib/triExplorer';
  initTriExplorers();
</script>
